Pad the left edge of a centred tab label

The rectangle of a tab label loses the tab pad at its right edge under
every alignment. The centred alignment adds the pad at the left edge
only while a button stands there. A centred label therefore sits three
pixels left of the centre of the tab, which is half of the pad.

The rectangle now takes the pad at the left edge while no button stands
there. The label sits at the centre of the tab. A tab with a left button
keeps the rectangle of before, and the left alignment does not move.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 17 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

